TY  - JOUR
TI  - Capivasertib in Hormone Receptor-Positive Advanced Breast Cancer
AU  - Turner, Nicholas C.
AU  - Oliveira, Mafalda
AU  - Howell, Sacha J.
AU  - Dalenc, Florence
AB  - BACKGROUND: Capivasertib is an inhibitor of the AKT kinases. METHODS: In this phase 3, randomized, double-blind trial, adults with hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative advanced breast cancer that had relapsed or progressed during or after aromatase inhibitor therapy were assigned to capivasertib plus fulvestrant or placebo plus fulvestrant. The dual primary end point was progression-free survival in the overall population and in patients with AKT pathway-altered tumours (PIK3CA, AKT1, or PTEN alterations). RESULTS: Progression-free survival was longer with capivasertib plus fulvestrant in both populations. (CAPItello-291 ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT04305496.)
PY  - 2023
DO  - 10.1056/NEJMoa2214131
JO  - The New England journal of medicine
AN  - 37256976
ER  - 

TY  - JOUR
TI  - Fulvestrant plus capivasertib versus placebo after relapse or progression on an aromatase inhibitor in metastatic, oestrogen receptor-positive breast cancer (FAKTION): a multicentre, randomised, controlled, phase 2 trial
AU  - Jones, Robert H.
AU  - Casbard, Angela
AU  - Carucci, Margherita
AB  - BACKGROUND: Activation of the PI3K/AKT pathway is common in oestrogen receptor-positive breast cancer. METHODS: In this randomised, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial, postmenopausal women with oestrogen receptor-positive, HER2-negative metastatic breast cancer that relapsed or progressed on an aromatase inhibitor were assigned to fulvestrant plus capivasertib or fulvestrant plus placebo. The primary endpoint was progression-free survival in the overall population. FINDINGS: Progression-free survival was longer with capivasertib. This study is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT01992952.
PY  - 2020
DO  - 10.1016/S1470-2045(19)30817-4
JO  - The Lancet. Oncology
AN  - 31987691
